      "sha256": "a12ecdd703cae75a6895e2cc10b41e5a13d4f408e220a17b3851bd10c31f198b",
      "output": "CAP-MODEL-01 PASS — peak sizing (21 channels) exceeds flat-day sizing (2), cooldown costs capacity, partial channels round up, and overlapping programmes sum\r\nCAP-SENS-02 PASS — 27 corners give 7..72 channels; the input that moves it most is dailyOrders (spread 32.3 channels)\r\nCAP-CALIB-03 PASS_UNCALIBRATED — the model declares itself uncalibrated and names W-0008 as the work that would calibrate it; no document relabels P5-3 as call evidence\r\nCAP-ALERT-04 PASS_WITH_NOT_PROVEN=COST_METRIC — prod ships 32 channels against a modelled peak of 21, and the ladder is monotonic (dev=4, staging=8, lab=12, prod=32). IvrConfirmationDeadlineMissed is zero-tolerance on ivr_missed_deadline_total, which the shipped pool justifies. cost_per_confirmed_order stays uninstrumented: 6/6 cost inputs are still blocked on a vendor quote (W-0008)\r\nCAP-DRIFT-05 PASS_DECLARED_DISAGREEMENT — model occupancy 40s, spec full-cycle 50s, runtime occupancy estimate 60s (read back from SchedulerCapacity.cs). They disagree by design and W-0008 is the work that would settle them\r\nCAP-SESSION-06 PASS_UNANSWERED — session length is declared open under M8-OD-C and the model still sizes against policy.windowSeconds. Substituting the unsourced 45-minute figure would take Golden Hour from 16 to 2 channels, so a session length is refused unless an arrival profile is decided with it\r\nCAPACITY_SELFTEST_PASS_UNCALIBRATED — the arithmetic is checked, the answer is a range, and the inputs are assumptions nobody has measured. This model must not drive a purchase until W-0008 produces a measured call duration."
    },
